Approved, subject to the following conditions:
1. That the structure’s setback be adjusted to be in line with the historic structure
at 1208 E Cannon;
2. That the driveway be moved to Tennessee Ave to reflect typical locations of a
driveway for corner lots;
3. That the uncovered slab on the right elevation be removed from the porch;
4. That the structure be raised to accommodate at least two 7” risers for the
porch to be consistent with the historic character in the area and a porch section
be submitted for review;
5. That the boxed eaves be changed to open rafters to be consistent with eaves
in the area;
6. That all windows reflect a traditional 1/1 configuration and an additional
window be placed on the right-side elevation;
7. That the cladding material be changed to reflect a typical lap siding material
for the area; and,
8. That any adjustments made to the drawings be submitted to the Development
Services Department prior to the issuance of a Certificate of Appropriateness.

Approved, subject to the following conditions:
1. That the multiple gables at the front be simplified;
2. That the roof pitch be lowered to reflect a more consistent with the historic
character;
3. That the windows be simplified to a 1/1 configuration;
4. That the reveal of the siding be marked on the plans; and
5. That any adjustments made to the drawings be submitted to the Development
Services Department prior to the issuance of a Certificate of Appropriateness.
